Installed `FinancialChart` (`@/components/ui/financial-chart`), a React wrapper over [Lightweight Charts](https://github.com/tradingview/lightweight-charts) 5.2.1 (`lightweight-charts`, Apache-2.0). Its NOTICE ("TradingView Lightweight Charts™, Copyright (с) 2025 TradingView, Inc. https://www.tradingview.com/") and license are at the end of the file; keep them.

```tsx
import { FinancialChart, type FinancialChartDatum } from "@/components/ui/financial-chart";

const candles: FinancialChartDatum[] = [
  { time: "2026-01-05", open: 100, high: 102.4, low: 99.1, close: 101.8, volume: 812000 },
  // ...
];

<FinancialChart label="Sample asset, daily prices" data={candles} series="area" height={320} />
```

The chart is created once per `series` and `volume` choice; new `data` is set in place (the view refits when the first time changes, so appended points keep the visitor's zoom). For live updates, use `ref.current.getSeries()?.update(point)`.

Attribution: the license asks you to show the NOTICE's attribution and a link to https://www.tradingview.com/ on the page that uses the chart. The chart's attribution logo (on by default, `options.layout.attributionLogo`) is that link; leave it on, or show the link yourself if you turn it off.

Theme it with the `--financial-chart-*` tokens: background, foreground (axis text), grid, border (scale borders), crosshair, crosshair-label, up, down, line, area-line, area-top, area-bottom, volume-up and volume-down. The light values are the library's defaults; the chart reads them again when the page's theme or color scheme changes. Tokens may use any CSS color (oklch included).
